  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>find_duplicates - finds near-duplicate products in ../catalog.csv by meaning, and has the model confirm
each pair.
Needs index_catalog run first, Ollama with ${MODEL_NAME} and nomic-embed-text, the pcm-pgvector
container and a GENAI-EE license.

1. csvi-catalog, js-embed-text, emb-catalog: as in index_catalog (no ID or metadata needed here).
2. vs-similar: Vector Search, PGVector table catalog_items, Max results ${TOP_K}, Min score
   ${MIN_SCORE}, dimension 768, One row per match, metadata product_id to match_product_id and title
   to match_title.
3. js-pair: Modified JavaScript value, drops the product's match with itself, keeps match_score &gt;=
   ${DUP_THRESHOLD} (is_pair Y), puts the pair in order (product_a &lt; product_b) and builds prompt from
   both embed_texts.
4. flt-pairs: Filter rows, is_pair = Y.
5. srt-pairs: Sort rows on product_a, product_b, only unique rows: each pair is found from both sides, kept
   once.
6. const-instruction: Add constants, run_instruction: same product, or different size, capacity, gender,
   garment or model; answer in JSON.
7. ai-same: AI Chat, Stream, message prompt, instruction run_instruction, Ollama ${MODEL_NAME},
   temperature 0, numCtx 2048, timeout 120, result llm_json.
8. json-same: JSON input from llm_json: same_product, reason. Error hop to txt-bad-answers
   (bad_pair_answers.csv).
9. sv-pairs, txt-pairs: duplicate_candidates.csv beside this file: product_a, product_b, title_a, title_b,
   match_score, same_product, reason.

Parameters: TOP_K 3, MIN_SCORE 0.9, DUP_THRESHOLD 0.93; change them in Run Options.</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>630</width>
      <heigth>458</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
